  <item>
    <title>EP04 二十五岁的当下，我们聊了时间、爱情与过往的一切</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/6288c81e83ddae2d9e72a884</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">6288c81e83ddae2d9e72a884</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 May 2022 11:08:10 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><strong><span>值班编辑：尧锋 阿忘</span></strong></p><span></span><h2><span>【编辑谈】</span></h2><span></span><p><span>“我实在想象不出自己25岁到30岁的样子，所以从现在到30岁之间的日子，我都打算告诉别人，我25岁。”</span></p><span></span><p><span>“我一直觉得喜欢比爱要难得多。”</span></p><span></span><p><span>“人生就是不断在走下坡路。”</span></p><span></span><p><span>这其实是莎士比亚那一期的副产品，是见缝插针的一些闲聊。然而我们都没想到，这些散碎的“跑题”，竟然多到能够撑起一期的内容量。</span></p><span></span><p><span>我们聊了童年的影像记忆，聊了少年轻狂的期许和成年之后的灰头土脸，也讨论了到底为什么成年人的世界复杂得没有必要，谈恋爱那么进退两难。这些当时当刻的“自我剖白”，即使是在回听的时候，某些想法都已经变了。不过我们还是尽量地保留了能够这些“入戏”瞬间，为终将到来的30岁留下参考坐标。</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>不知道你对自己的25岁，有过怎样的想象？或者说，回望25岁，你最想分享的是什么故事？欢迎留言讨论。感谢收听。</span></strong></p><span></span><h2><span>【目录】</span></h2><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="69">01:09</a> 纸制品承载的回忆</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="133">02:13</a> 惊悚的自觉</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="200">03:20</a> 下一站，三十</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="235">03:55</a> 忧伤的“二十五”体验</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="320">05:20</a> 二十五岁的我，如何走过那十年</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="366">06:06</a> 聊以自慰的人生下坡路</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="460">07:40</a> 展开的未来</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="515">08:35</a> 与文学同构的自我</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="650">10:50</a> “光环散去”的当下</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="772">12:52</a> 世人皆爱伤仲永的故事</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="873">14:33</a> 初中同学聚会的三两事</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1167">19:27</a> 与价值相比，礼物的巧思更重要</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1230">20:30</a> 被疫情耽误的高中同学会</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1365">22:45</a> 争奇斗艳与各自的变化</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1445">24:05</a> 最近看的影视</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1631">27:11</a> 回归原著的邓布利多</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1725">28:45</a> 纽特与邓布利多：亦师亦友</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1790">29:50</a> 哈利与邓布利多：精神弑父</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1932">32:12</a> 幽微的情感关系</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1966">32:46</a> 爱比喜欢更容易</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2012">33:32</a> 喜欢是非理性的</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2113">35:13</a> 爱不一定是排他的</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2173">36:13</a> 爱有分别吗？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2307">38:27</a> 有些情境让人压力山大</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2398">39:58</a> 两性如战场</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2453">40:53</a> 莎士比亚的爱情教育</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2503">41:43</a> 为了不存在的东西而互相折磨</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2740">45:40</a> 不愿意谈心的背后，另有隐情</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2801">46:41</a> 谈恋爱这件事，大同小异</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2956">49:16</a> 没有主见，结果可能很可怕</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3135">52:15</a> 中国人的实用主义，体现在婚姻</span></p><span></span><h2><span>【BGM】</span></h2><span></span><p><span>Impromptus, Op. 90 D. 899: No. 1 en ut mineur - Alexandre Tharaud</span></p><span></span><p><span>Bolerisch (From Femme Fatale) - 坂本龍一</span></p><span></span><p><span>クロニクル - 岩井俊二</span></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/llVjpixnDicn4EjBsM_LNAtabo4a.m4a" length="78900592" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:53:41</itunes:duration>
    <itunes:image href="https://bts-image.xyzcdn.net/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWFnZS54eXpjZG4ubmV0L2xpNTV0VEJRcEo4MTdfUU9ITjY5WU1ONWMtUEQucG5n.png"/>
    <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>EP03 世界阅读日，让我们谈回莎士比亚</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/6263ec026e11ff9a9f9a9987</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">6263ec026e11ff9a9f9a9987</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 23 Apr 2022 12:07:26 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><strong><span>值班编辑：尧锋 阿忘</span></strong></p><span></span><h2><span>【编辑谈】</span></h2><span></span><p><span>今天是世界阅读日，亦是剧作家威廉·莎士比亚的诞辰与忌日。莎士比亚的作品繁多而丰富，覆盖了无数的主题，对英语语言与文学的影响持续至今。于是今天要来和大家聊聊莎士比亚，聊聊他的爱情观，聊聊他如何看待政治，再聊聊他如何处理宗教、哲学和时代议题。</span></p><span></span><p><span>让我们来聊聊关于莎士比亚的一切。</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>如果本期节目有你感兴趣的话题，欢迎留言讨论。感谢收听。</span></strong></p><span></span><h2><span>【目录】</span></h2><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="99">01:39</a> 莎士比亚给大家的“爱情教育”与女性观</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1274">21:14</a> 莎士比亚的宗教复杂性</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1735">28:55</a> 哈姆雷特的哲学迷思</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2823">47:03</a> 莎士比亚或许也是悲观主义者？！</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3415">56:55</a> 莎士比亚与剧场形态</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4326">1:12:06</a> 《裘力斯·凯撒》：政治就是一场表演</span></p><span></span><h2><span>【BGM】</span></h2><span></span><p><span>Impromptus, Op. 90 D. 899: No. 1 en ut mineur - Alexandre Tharaud</span></p><span></span><p><span>Mad Rush - Philip Glass</span></p><span></span><p><span>Hallelujah Junction - 1st movement - John Adams</span></p><span></span><p><span>M.A.Y. in the Backyard - Ryuichi Sakamoto</span></p><span></span><p><span>La Javanaise - Madeleine Peyroux</span></p>]]></description>
